{"module":"christian-nationalism","voice":"female","duration":226.2,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Christian nationalism and race","start":0.0,"end":2.24,"words":[[0.05,0.67],[0.67,1.52],[1.52,1.76],[1.76,2.07]]},{"el":"intro","text":"This module is not about Christianity, which has been on every side of this history (see “Faith”).","start":3.04,"end":8.56,"words":[[3.09,3.29],[3.29,3.69],[3.69,3.83],[3.83,4.03],[4.03,4.37],[4.37,5.24],[5.47,5.74],[5.74,5.94],[5.94,6.15],[6.15,6.28],[6.28,6.55],[6.55,6.82],[6.82,6.95],[6.95,7.15],[7.15,7.62],[7.62,7.76],[7.76,8.09]]},{"el":"intro","text":"It is about a specific political idea: that the United States is, and should be, a Christian nation, with laws and power that favor one group.","start":8.91,"end":18.92,"words":[[8.96,9.11],[9.11,9.26],[9.26,9.64],[9.64,9.79],[9.79,10.4],[10.4,11.08],[11.08,11.54],[11.8,12.03],[12.03,12.18],[12.18,12.79],[12.79,13.25],[13.25,13.48],[13.74,13.97],[13.97,14.2],[14.2,14.43],[14.69,14.84],[14.84,15.45],[15.45,15.98],[16.25,16.48],[16.48,16.71],[16.71,16.93],[16.93,17.24],[17.24,17.47],[17.47,17.85],[17.85,18.07],[18.07,18.45]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Researchers measure it with surveys, and they disagree about some of what it means.","start":19.27,"end":24.06,"words":[[19.32,19.89],[19.89,20.17],[20.17,20.31],[20.31,20.52],[20.52,21.01],[21.25,21.46],[21.46,21.67],[21.67,22.16],[22.16,22.51],[22.51,22.72],[22.72,22.86],[22.86,23.07],[23.07,23.21],[23.21,23.56]]},{"el":"h0","text":"What researchers mean","start":24.41,"end":25.73,"words":[[24.46,24.71],[24.71,25.38],[25.38,25.64]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Sociologists Andrew Whitehead and Samuel Perry define Christian nationalism as a belief that America is and should be a Christian nation, measured by agreement with statements such as “the federal government should declare the United States a Christian nation.”","start":26.43,"end":41.83,"words":[[26.48,27.54],[27.54,27.9],[27.9,28.39],[28.39,28.6],[28.6,29.03],[29.03,29.31],[29.31,29.73],[29.73,30.3],[30.3,31.08],[31.08,31.22],[31.22,31.36],[31.36,31.71],[31.71,31.93],[31.93,32.42],[32.42,32.56],[32.56,32.77],[32.77,32.99],[32.99,33.13],[33.13,33.27],[33.27,33.83],[33.83,34.33],[34.58,34.93],[34.93,35.14],[35.14,35.71],[35.71,35.92],[35.92,36.63],[36.63,36.91],[36.91,37.05],[37.05,37.19],[37.19,37.69],[37.69,38.32],[38.32,38.54],[38.54,38.96],[38.96,39.1],[39.1,39.67],[39.67,40.09],[40.09,40.23],[40.23,40.8],[40.8,41.29]]},{"el":"s0","text":"In a 2023 national survey by PRRI, about 10% of Americans qualified as adherents and another 19% as sympathizers, so most Americans, and most Christians, are neither.","start":42.18,"end":55.77,"words":[[42.24,42.38],[42.38,42.52],[42.52,43.6],[43.6,44.1],[44.1,44.45],[44.45,44.67],[44.67,45.38],[45.63,45.99],[45.99,46.64],[46.64,46.78],[46.78,47.42],[47.42,48.07],[48.07,48.21],[48.21,48.93],[48.93,49.14],[49.14,49.5],[49.5,50.43],[50.43,50.57],[50.57,51.43],[51.68,51.9],[51.9,52.25],[52.25,52.97],[53.22,53.43],[53.43,53.79],[53.79,54.51],[54.76,54.83],[54.83,55.26]]},{"el":"h1","text":"A long history","start":56.67,"end":58.11,"words":[[56.72,56.94],[56.94,57.26],[57.26,58.01]]},{"el":"s1","text":"The Ku Klux Klan of the 1920s, with millions of members, presented itself as the defender of white Protestant America against Black people, Catholics, Jews and immigrants, and burned crosses as a religious symbol.","start":58.81,"end":73.45,"words":[[58.85,59.0],[59.0,59.15],[59.15,59.52],[59.52,59.81],[59.81,59.96],[59.96,60.11],[60.11,61.22],[61.48,61.7],[61.7,62.22],[62.22,62.37],[62.37,62.88],[63.14,63.81],[63.81,64.25],[64.25,64.4],[64.4,64.55],[64.55,65.07],[65.07,65.22],[65.22,65.51],[65.51,66.25],[66.25,66.77],[66.77,67.21],[67.21,67.51],[67.51,67.95],[68.21,68.8],[69.06,69.36],[69.36,69.58],[69.58,70.32],[70.58,70.8],[70.8,71.1],[71.1,71.54],[71.54,71.69],[71.69,71.84],[71.84,72.43],[72.43,72.95]]},{"el":"s1","text":"During the civil rights era, some prominent preachers taught that segregation was God's will; Bob Jones Sr. preached a 1960 Easter sermon titled “Is Segregation Scriptural?” and answered yes.","start":73.8,"end":86.75,"words":[[73.84,74.34],[74.34,74.48],[74.48,74.83],[74.83,75.18],[75.18,75.54],[75.79,76.0],[76.0,76.63],[76.63,77.13],[77.13,77.34],[77.34,77.55],[77.55,78.33],[78.33,78.54],[78.54,78.82],[78.82,79.11],[79.35,79.57],[79.57,79.99],[79.99,80.27],[80.63,81.05],[81.05,81.19],[81.19,82.11],[82.11,82.39],[82.39,82.75],[82.75,83.24],[83.24,83.38],[83.38,84.16],[84.16,85.01],[85.36,85.57],[85.57,85.93],[85.93,86.21]]},{"el":"s1","text":"The white-supremacist Christian Identity movement is covered in “Before race.”","start":87.1,"end":92.1,"words":[[87.15,87.3],[87.3,88.41],[88.41,89.0],[89.0,89.67],[89.67,90.19],[90.19,90.34],[90.34,90.71],[90.71,90.86],[90.86,91.15],[91.15,91.52]]},{"el":"h2","text":"How did the religious right begin?","start":93.0,"end":94.96,"words":[[93.02,93.2],[93.2,93.37],[93.37,93.49],[93.49,93.96],[93.96,94.2],[94.2,94.55]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Historian Randall Balmer argues that conservative evangelicals first organized politically in the 1970s not over abortion but to defend the tax exemptions of private Christian schools that excluded Black students, many founded as “segregation academies.”","start":95.66,"end":113.75,"words":[[95.7,96.44],[96.44,96.93],[96.93,97.25],[97.25,97.66],[97.66,97.9],[97.9,98.72],[98.72,99.78],[99.78,100.1],[100.1,100.76],[100.76,101.49],[101.49,101.65],[101.65,101.82],[101.82,103.04],[103.04,103.28],[103.28,103.61],[103.61,104.1],[104.1,104.34],[104.34,104.5],[104.5,104.99],[104.99,105.16],[105.16,105.48],[105.48,106.3],[106.3,106.46],[106.46,107.03],[107.03,107.68],[107.68,108.09],[108.09,108.34],[108.34,109.07],[109.07,109.39],[109.39,110.21],[110.5,110.82],[110.82,111.39],[111.39,111.55],[111.55,112.45],[112.45,113.18]]},{"el":"s2","text":"The Supreme Court upheld revoking Bob Jones University's exemption over its ban on interracial dating in 1983.","start":114.1,"end":121.62,"words":[[114.15,114.29],[114.29,114.72],[114.72,114.93],[114.93,115.35],[115.35,115.92],[115.92,116.13],[116.13,116.55],[116.55,117.33],[117.33,117.96],[117.96,118.25],[118.25,118.46],[118.46,118.67],[118.67,118.81],[118.81,119.52],[119.52,119.94],[119.94,120.08],[120.08,121.14]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Other historians stress abortion, school prayer and changing family norms.","start":121.97,"end":127.26,"words":[[122.02,122.26],[122.26,123.04],[123.04,123.43],[123.43,123.98],[124.26,124.57],[124.57,124.88],[124.88,125.12],[125.12,125.82],[125.82,126.29],[126.29,126.68]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Both sides agree the school fight was one of the movement's early causes.","start":127.61,"end":131.89,"words":[[127.67,127.96],[127.96,128.32],[128.32,128.62],[128.62,128.76],[128.76,129.06],[129.06,129.35],[129.35,129.57],[129.57,129.79],[129.79,129.93],[129.93,130.08],[130.08,130.66],[130.66,130.88],[130.88,131.32]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Is it linked to racial attitudes?","start":132.79,"end":134.8,"words":[[132.84,132.96],[132.96,133.07],[133.07,133.37],[133.37,133.48],[133.48,133.83],[133.83,134.36]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Whitehead and Perry report that people who score high on Christian nationalism are more likely to say police treat Black and white Americans equally and to oppose measures to address racial inequality, even after accounting for party and religiosity.","start":135.5,"end":151.64,"words":[[135.56,136.14],[136.14,136.39],[136.39,136.72],[136.72,137.14],[137.14,137.39],[137.39,137.81],[137.81,137.97],[137.97,138.22],[138.22,138.47],[138.47,138.64],[138.64,139.3],[139.3,140.22],[140.22,140.3],[140.3,140.47],[140.47,140.97],[140.97,141.13],[141.13,141.38],[141.38,141.8],[141.8,142.13],[142.13,142.47],[142.47,142.72],[142.72,143.05],[143.05,143.8],[143.8,144.3],[144.3,144.55],[144.55,144.71],[144.71,145.13],[145.13,145.54],[145.54,145.71],[145.71,146.13],[146.13,146.63],[146.63,147.54],[147.83,148.16],[148.16,148.5],[148.5,149.16],[149.16,149.33],[149.33,149.66],[149.66,149.91],[149.91,151.08]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Critics question how the concept is measured and whether surveys can separate it from political conservatism.","start":151.99,"end":158.52,"words":[[152.05,152.55],[152.55,153.12],[153.12,153.33],[153.33,153.48],[153.48,153.98],[153.98,154.12],[154.12,154.48],[154.48,154.69],[154.69,154.98],[154.98,155.41],[155.41,155.62],[155.62,156.05],[156.05,156.2],[156.2,156.48],[156.48,157.13],[157.13,158.06]]},{"el":"s3","text":"The pattern appears in several data sets; how to interpret it is debated.","start":158.87,"end":163.76,"words":[[158.92,159.07],[159.07,159.44],[159.44,159.81],[159.81,159.95],[159.95,160.39],[160.39,160.76],[160.76,161.13],[161.39,161.61],[161.61,161.75],[161.75,162.34],[162.34,162.49],[162.49,162.63],[162.63,163.3]]},{"el":"h4","text":"Recent events","start":164.66,"end":165.9,"words":[[164.72,165.26],[165.26,165.79]]},{"el":"s4","text":"During the January 6, 2021 attack on the Capitol, some participants carried crosses, “Jesus Saves” signs and Christian flags alongside Confederate flags, and a group prayed on the Senate floor.","start":166.6,"end":180.59,"words":[[166.65,167.18],[167.18,167.34],[167.34,168.02],[168.02,168.4],[168.66,169.8],[169.8,170.1],[170.1,170.26],[170.26,170.41],[170.41,171.01],[171.28,171.51],[171.51,172.34],[172.34,172.72],[172.72,173.25],[173.52,173.97],[173.97,174.35],[174.35,174.73],[174.73,174.96],[174.96,175.56],[175.56,175.94],[175.94,176.55],[176.55,177.31],[177.31,177.76],[178.03,178.25],[178.25,178.41],[178.41,178.71],[178.71,179.09],[179.09,179.24],[179.24,179.39],[179.39,179.77],[179.77,180.07]]},{"el":"s4","text":"A 2022 report by the Baptist Joint Committee and the Freedom From Religion Foundation documented these symbols and the groups behind them.","start":180.94,"end":189.76,"words":[[181.0,181.14],[181.14,182.11],[182.11,182.45],[182.45,182.66],[182.66,182.8],[182.8,183.28],[183.28,183.69],[183.69,184.11],[184.11,184.31],[184.31,184.45],[184.45,184.87],[184.87,185.14],[185.14,185.69],[185.69,186.38],[186.38,187.14],[187.14,187.35],[187.35,187.83],[187.83,188.04],[188.04,188.18],[188.18,188.52],[188.52,189.0],[189.0,189.28]]},{"el":"h5","text":"Christians who oppose it","start":190.66,"end":192.14,"words":[[190.7,191.33],[191.33,191.47],[191.47,191.82],[191.82,191.96]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Tens of thousands of Christians, including many clergy, have signed the “Christians Against Christian Nationalism” statement launched by the Baptist Joint Committee for Religious Liberty in 2019, which says it “distorts both the Christian faith and America's constitutional democracy.”","start":192.84,"end":210.92,"words":[[192.89,193.18],[193.18,193.33],[193.33,193.91],[193.91,194.06],[194.06,194.79],[195.04,195.63],[195.63,195.92],[195.92,196.43],[196.68,196.9],[196.9,197.27],[197.27,197.41],[197.41,198.07],[198.07,198.51],[198.51,199.09],[199.09,199.89],[199.89,200.55],[200.55,200.99],[200.99,201.2],[201.2,201.35],[201.35,201.86],[201.86,202.3],[202.3,202.74],[202.74,202.88],[202.88,203.47],[203.47,203.9],[203.9,204.05],[204.05,205.07],[205.33,205.62],[205.62,205.84],[205.84,205.98],[205.98,206.49],[206.49,206.78],[206.78,206.93],[206.93,207.51],[207.51,207.8],[207.8,208.02],[208.02,208.61],[208.61,209.63],[209.63,210.36]]},{"el":"s5","text":"The Black church, the Poor People's Campaign and many denominations have long argued that faith requires equal protection for everyone.","start":211.27,"end":220.92,"words":[[211.32,211.49],[211.49,211.84],[211.84,212.37],[212.68,212.85],[212.85,213.11],[213.11,213.64],[213.64,214.25],[214.25,214.51],[214.51,214.86],[214.86,216.0],[216.0,216.26],[216.26,216.53],[216.53,216.97],[216.97,217.23],[217.23,217.58],[217.58,218.28],[218.28,218.72],[218.72,219.5],[219.5,219.68],[219.68,220.38]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Faith communities are often the most credible voices on this subject.","start":221.27,"end":225.34,"words":[[221.3,221.56],[221.56,222.22],[222.22,222.29],[222.29,222.56],[222.56,222.69],[222.69,223.02],[223.02,223.55],[223.55,223.95],[223.95,224.08],[224.08,224.28],[224.28,224.88]]}]}